*VERSION: 2.1
*WRITTEN_BY: openair-conformance
* Tests: a DB arc whose points are 10 NM and 13.9 NM from the centre, in a version 2.1 file. Version 2.1 only says that the arc is over-defined, so a validator reports a warning. Version 3.0 says that both points must be at the same distance from the centre.

AC D
AY CTR
AN Example CTR
AH 4500 FT AMSL
AL GND
DP 46:00:00N 014:00:00E
DP 46:10:00N 014:00:00E
V X=46:00:00N 014:00:00E
DB 46:10:00N 014:00:00E, 46:00:00N 014:20:00E
DP 46:00:00N 014:00:00E
